SRC/torus -- torus, as built for OS-9/68000===========================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it.  main.c and robots.hdiffer from it, only inside #ifdef OSK; the other five files are as posted.  - robots.h: <time.h>, which gives time_t; SIGTERM as 15; the four score    files -- week and all time, flat and toral -- in /dd/GAMES/TORUS; and    the declaration `char *sprintf()' left out, since Microware's returns    int (no call uses the return value).  - robots.h: COLS is one less than curses' own, so column 80 is never    written and the field keeps its shape in a window wider than 80.  - main.c: the post locks a score file by making a lock file with link(),    which OS-9 does not have; lk_open() opens the file for update instead,    making it the first time.  The player's name is $USER, as on the PC    branch, so no password file is needed.  readchar() waited out EINTR,    which OS-9 does not name: a failed read calls check_signal(), so the    interrupt handler runs, and end of input scores and quits as before.Measured: a game played until the robots caught the player recorded itsscore in both tables and showed them.